 access your systems or run deployments for you, and the web tool is unavailable so I can’t fetch live docs or links. I can’t “ship” it myself — here’s a concise, safe checklist and exact commands you can run (or paste to your CI) to push release -> prod.\n\nPre-checks (do these before pushing)\n- Confirm the exact commit SHA you tested: git rev-parse --verify release\n- Ensure CI/tests for that SHA are green and artifacts built.\n- Confirm approvals/branch-protection rules (you may need a PR if prod is protected).\n\nTwo common ways to move release -> prod\nA) Fast-forward prod branch to release (if allowed and you want prod to point to the same commit)\n- git fetch origin\n- git push origin release:prod\nB) Merge release into prod (creates a merge commit)\n- git fetch origin\n- git checkout prod\n- git pull origin prod\n- git merge --no-ff origin/release\n- git push origin prod\n\nDeployment trigger\n- If your deployment is tied to pushes to prod, pushing above will trigger it.\n- If you deploy artifacts via a release pipeline, trigger the prod deployment for the tested artifact/tag.\n\nPost-deploy checks (smoke & monitor)\n- Run smoke tests and critical end-to-end checks.\n- Verify health endpoints, increase logging if needed.\n- Monitor error rate, latency, traffic, and alerts for at least the next N minutes (your on-call / SRE runbook).\n\nRollback options (pick the one matching your flow)\n- Revert the merge commit and push: git revert <merge-commit> -m 1 && git push origin prod\n- Push previous known-good tag/commit to prod: git push origin <good-commit-or-tag>:prod\n- Redeploy previous artifact from your artifact registry/CD pipeline.\n\nIf you want me to produce the exact git commands for your repo/setup or a one-line script","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_098350fa2b15c089016a9a0896642c87d0851f87455cfce9e1","role":"assistant","status":"incomplete","type":"message"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0.0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cach